message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "Census of AI / Frontier-Model Partnerships across the 2026 Formula 1 Grid"
authors:
  - family-names: "Wang"
    given-names: "Hanyu"
    email: "hw3592@nyu.edu"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-2336-7057"
version: "1.5"
date-released: "2026-08-01"
license: CC-BY-4.0
# The Zenodo release is deliberately held until the companion paper is posted, so the
# concept DOI does not exist yet. Uncomment and fill it after the first release, using the
# CONCEPT doi (not the version doi) so citations always resolve to the latest version.
# doi: "10.5281/zenodo.0000000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hildahanyuwang/f1-ai-partnership-census"
abstract: >-
  A hand-built, primary-source census of publicly disclosed artificial-intelligence,
  cloud, data, semiconductor, cybersecurity and enterprise-software partnerships held
  by the eleven 2026 Formula 1 teams (plus the driver-personal and F1-central
  landscape). Each of the 105 arrangements is coded for whether the FIA cost cap's
  valuation machinery can price it (a two-tier scheme built on three economic
  properties: bidirectional value flow, no clearing price, capability drift), for
  integration depth, activity class, and disclosure of financial terms, with an
  individually verified primary-source URL per record. Companion dataset to a study
  of frontier AI and spending-based competitive regulation.
keywords:
  - Formula 1
  - cost cap
  - artificial intelligence
  - frontier AI
  - sponsorship
  - competitive regulation
  - sports economics
  - valuation
  - dataset census
